---
import { getCollection } from 'astro:content';
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { SITE_NAME, CONTACT_EMAIL, DATA_DATE_LABEL } from '../lib/site';

const listings = await getCollection('listings');
const jsonLd = [{
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'AboutPage',
  name: `About ${SITE_NAME}`,
  mainEntity: { '@type': 'Organization', name: SITE_NAME, email: CONTACT_EMAIL ?? undefined, parentOrganization: { '@type': 'Organization', name: 'PALM ICON LLC' } },
}];
---
<BaseLayout title="About This Site and Who Runs It | Charter Prices Compared" description="Who runs Private Jet Charter Prices Compared, why it exists, how it is paid for, and what it has and has not done." jsonLd={jsonLd}>
  <div class="wrap prose">
    <p class="crumbs"><a href="/">Home</a> / About</p>
    <h1>Who runs this site, and why it exists</h1>
    <p class="lead">Charter prices are hard to compare because every provider publishes a different number under the same label. This site puts those numbers side by side, with the page each one came from.</p>

    <h2>Who runs it</h2>
    <p>{SITE_NAME} is operated by PALM ICON LLC in Miami, Florida. It is an independent site. No listed provider owns it, pays to be listed, or reviews what we write about them before it is published.</p>
    {CONTACT_EMAIL && <p>You can reach us at <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>.</p>}

    <h2>What we did</h2>
    <p>On {DATA_DATE_LABEL} we read the public pages of {listings.length} private jet charter providers and recorded what each says about price, fees and whether it flies the aircraft itself. Every listing links to the pages we read. We checked the federal tax figures against the FAA's own 2026 document.</p>

    <h2>What we did not do</h2>
    <p>We did not request quotes, call providers, use their booking tools or fly with them. We have not tested any provider, and nothing here is a recommendation to book with one. Published rates are marketing figures. Your trip will price differently, which is why the site shows you what to ask for in writing.</p>

    <h2>How the site is paid for</h2>
    <p>Some links are affiliate links. We have applied to the affiliate programs of some providers, and Villiers has approved us, so the link on its listing is an affiliate link. Others are still in review. Affiliate links are marked as sponsored in the page code, disclosed next to the link and on the <a href="/affiliate-disclosure/">affiliate disclosure</a> page. Whether a provider has a program does not decide whether it is listed, where it appears or what we say about it. Providers are in alphabetical order.</p>

    <h2>If we got something wrong</h2>
    <p>Tell us, and we will check it against the provider's page and fix it. The process, and a log of every correction, is on the <a href="/corrections/">corrections page</a>. Providers are welcome to send corrections to their own listing.</p>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
